<description>&lt;p&gt;Communal and inter-clan violence continues across South Sudan, with armed men killing civilians on the Juba-Bor road, a raid in Yirol West killing dozens, and a cattle raid in the Eastern Lakes region leaving 20 dead. The SSPDF reported neutralizing a SPLA-IO/NAS commander linked to a massacre of 36 people in Khor Gal-tan, while the Upper Nile governor condemned an attack that killed 23 in Ulang County. Political pressure mounts as the president gave Machar a 48‑hour deadline to return and the UN condemned the surge in violence. The multi-donor ResPEct project ended its four-year effort to combat gender-based violence. Two battle-related deaths were recorded in 2024, according to UCDP.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;Machine-written from the linked sources, checked for figures and names not in them.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://news.google.com/rss/articles/CBMikwFBVV95cUxPV3c5dVRRcDBQSkl3azc5Z2drTTFlMjFCYllTY3ZTY0JST3g0bjlVb2VKYkRzMHdwbkNuZXVDTUJ2ZkNCS1FBeERoMFh5UUo5cFBCdTMyWmVBQlE1Slp5M251SEhjV0hkbk9lMFdrSDFOMWlOY1pnQmFvaEJXaEExaTdmSjhLdVpRblp4YU5paWc0VzA?oc=5&quot;&gt;ReliefWeb&lt;/a&gt;, &lt;a href=&quot;https://news.google.?oc=5&quot;&gt;Eye Radio&lt;/a&gt;, &lt;a href=&quot;https://news.google.com/rss/articles/CBMixgFBVV95cUxPVnNrN25BVXVlc0ViSkZvU3FaaEtScVlpNnVUTlNmOUNoOHBDXzloUGZ1TkpQdnVLUUZXN0l3NFdXbDVPQXFkZ25VTlJpdXlTVU8wTTdZektFMGFhemFyRjh1bWhZZms2aHV6NTUzSHFRc09aeTROaDNiWDdaY1V1MGQ2c09jZ04yNXZxckV0Y3ZnQ3JCM1duSldlWUJHc1NkOTdSOUhsaklRZ3Z4UEljcjB1V1hJTXVJUk9wNHUzdXJiSFNMbWc?oc=5&quot;&gt;streamlinefeed.co.ke&lt;/a&gt;, &lt;a href=&quot;https://news.google.?oc=5&quot;&gt;Eye Radio&lt;/a&gt;, &lt;a href=&quot;https://news.google.com/rss/articles/CBMipAFBVV95cUxPVXRkMWlLSUs2aDNZUWdLcmxybEFXV3RZY3ZmUlFaemQ0Mm1Pb1ZCRWdsc0JNYWJvVHY0clhvNHJWQzFOdkJlLTFWazdnTnFrVXR0d216aDBLejlkYWcyYTFuY0x1Y19tVDBwWnBEblV6RmZ3alVRTzVZWmdvMWNXWHJGQkdNenRvdUVPNmhEWFhoLThTdkszRnplYlVwbjdWN0dpMA?oc=5&quot;&gt;Africa Top Sports&lt;/a&gt;, &lt;a h